title ALES8 — Lotus's per-track fader column, balance the mix before it renders
prompt Continue the autonomous recur (baton prin recur): next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, self-approve design rounds, send each finished increment to origin and xykj61, STOP only at custody gates.
think Fourth increment of this recur, after ALES5 (clock), ALES6 (track table), ALES7 (transport) all landed and pushed. Read REMEMBER (custody gates — #1 seed force-push is Keaton's hand, done 20260812; nothing in reach), the 1,024-round itinerary and the six-season double-seat. The living git edge is the Lotus/ALES ladder — pure local software, no gate in reach.
think Lindy-first crux-first: of ALES7's named next roads (loop · scrub · crossfade curve · fader column), the fader column is the most durable — the mixer is the heart of every DAW, read on the ten-thousandth day. A transport loop only extends the read head ALES7 built; a crossfade curve refines the ALES4 fade. The ALES6 witness itself names the fader column by name. So the fader first.
think The one crux: a fader column cannot be gain-then-render, because ALES2's gain saturates each clip to i16 BEFORE it could join the sum — a double-clamp against the mix. The correctness a mixer owes is that the fader multiply happens INSIDE the accumulation, per sample in i64, so only the final sum meets floor and ceiling. Designed lotus/fader.rye: Fader{num,den} (default unity), make (BadGain on zero den), render(session, faders, clock, out) — each track scaled in the wide accumulator, saturate once, faders.len == session.count asserted, ClipFull/DurationTooLong forwarded exactly as ALES6.
think The sharpest proof is the mixer null test: a clip mixed with a copy of itself faded at -1/1 cancels to EXACT silence — only correct because the negative fader scales in the wide domain before the single clamp (acc holds v + (-v) = 0). Additive: ALES6's track.rye stands untouched, the column composes over its public API; a unity column reproduces track.render byte-for-byte (asserted against the real ALES6 render in the selftest).
obs GREEN on first build across seven blocks. tame_style_check bans clean (fader.rye carries ≥2 asserts per fn, not on the zero-assert ratchet), width-check exit 0, ALES6 track witness re-run GREEN (strictly additive). render's error union (TrackError || clock.ClockError || timeline.EditError) coerces the try calls cleanly.
obs Honest scope kept explicit: the fader is a validated num/den level, no electrical or hardware claim; purely local, no socket, no network, no keys, no funds, no real device. No custody gate reached.
loom witness=ales_fader_witness cases=7 build=first_green tame=clean width=exit0 ales6_regreen=1
file lotus/fader.rye ALES8 module — Fader/make/render, per-track level scaled in the wide accumulator, saturate once over the true faded sum
file tools/ales_fader_witness.rish witness — 7 cases (unity==ALES6, half, mute, boosted-saturate, -1 null, BadGain, ClipFull), GREEN on metal
file active-designing/20260814-fill-ales8-lotus-fader-column.md self-approved design round for ALES8
file lotus/README.md seated ALES8 in status, rungs, prove-list, road-on
recommend keep-going ALES9 — pan (a fader per channel as stereo opens), mute/solo as first-class session state, a transport loop over a marked region, or the equal-power crossfade curve. No custody gate in reach.
